attr[seg000:2e98]: name = set_command_menu_origin; comment = [[[
    Compute the verb-menu draw origin from the command_list header at di (= command_list_ptr) and save the list.
    command_menu_list = di; command_menu_x = header[0]; command_menu_y = header[1] + 0ch.
]]]
attr[seg000:2eb2]: name = ui_draw_room_command_panel; comment = [[[
    Draw the bottom command/dialogue panel (run via gfx_call_bp_with_front_buffer_as_screen).
    When a dialogue is active (data_04774 != 0) it renders the dialogue (loc_0301a); otherwise it builds and renders the verb menu for command_list_ptr:
    set_command_menu_origin -> build_room_command_records -> (room mode) build_persons_in_room_records,
    then rebuild_and_draw_room_nav_panel and the book/companion buttons (loc_0d763), and enqueues the record list (bp=1f0eh) into the draw-task list.
]]]
attr[seg000:2efb]: name = build_room_command_records; comment = [[[
    Assemble the verb-menu record list for the current room into the buffer at 1f0fh.
    Format: a leading 0 byte, then 4-byte [text_id:u16, handler_ofs:u16] records, then a 0 terminator word.
    The records are copied from the seg001 command-record templates (21dc..221c), gated by the room type (command_slot/data_00006 low byte 80h = special room), location_and_room, game_phase, orni_count, the smuggler flag, and time-of-day.
]]]
attr[seg000:2ffb]: name = rebuild_and_draw_room_nav_panel; comment = [[[
    Rebuild the bottom-right navigation/compass HUD records (12..18) for the current room context, then draw them (falls into loc_0d735).
    Night-attack / map / book modes pick alternate templates; the plain room uses the move-direction set keyed off command_list_ptr and location_and_room.
]]]
attr[seg000:3090]: name = build_persons_in_room_records; comment = [[[
    Append the people-present command records to the verb-menu list (called after build_room_command_records when game_screen_mode_flags == 0).
    Reset the per-scene lip-sync state, run init_room_persons to reset the four scene-person slots, clear persons_in_room, then walk the room-person table twice with scan_matching_room_person_entries: first with bp = build_room_person_record_a (entries whose flags bit 0x40 is clear), then with bp = build_room_person_record_b (entries whose flags bit 0x40 is set). Both templates share the body at build_room_person_record_body.
]]]
attr[seg000:30b9]: type = code; name = build_room_person_record_a; comment = [[[
    bp template A for scan_matching_room_person_entries (called from build_persons_in_room_records).
    Skip when entry flags [si+0fh] & 0x40 is set; on the first match (data_047aa == 0) record si into data_047aa so the room-screen tail picks it as the lip-sync speaker; then fall through to the shared body at loc_030ca.
]]]
attr[seg000:30ca]: name = build_room_person_record_body; comment = [[[
    Shared tail of build_room_person_record_a / _b.
    emit a verb-menu record (text_id = 0x78 + persons_met[si], handler = location_and_room[si] = [si+4]), OR (1 << cl) into persons_in_room, and, when cl == 0x0f, emit data_0476a-1 extra chained 0x88..0x8f records. When game_phase >= 5 and data_0476b is non-zero, patch one earlier record to text_id 0x8f.
]]]
attr[seg000:3120]: type = code; name = build_room_person_record_b; comment = [[[
    bp template B for scan_matching_room_person_entries (called from build_persons_in_room_records).
    Mirror of build_room_person_record_a with the flags-bit-0x40 test inverted: process only entries whose [si+0fh] & 0x40 is set by jumping to the shared body at loc_030ca, otherwise return without touching data_047aa.
    The static room_persons table has no bit-0x40 entries, so this only fires when game state writes the bit at runtime.
]]]
attr[seg000:3127]: name = init_room_persons; comment = [[[
    Reset the four scene person slots before build_persons_in_room_records scans the room-person table.
    Zero data_0476a and data_0476b, init the four person-state words at data_109a/10aa/10ba/10ca to 0x7f80, then (only when location_slot low byte == 0x80) classify entries by iterating the room-person table via loc_06603 with bp = loc_0316e, and run loc_0331e.
]]]
