attr[seg000:88af]: name = request_voice_subtitle; comment = [[[
    Entry point for displaying a voice/narration subtitle. ax = string id.
    Stores ax at current_subtitle_id (data_04780), clears data_047e0, then on the normal path:
    - get_phrase_or_command_string_si: resolve id -> COMMAND/PHRASE bytes
    - loc_088f1: expand phrase tokens (0xe0+) into temp buffer 0xa840
    - loc_088d2: format_interpolated_string -> 0xa6b0, then if voice_subtitle_mode < 2 draw via loc_088e1 -> loc_08b11.
    The data_046eb & 0x40 short-circuit drops the bubble entirely (loc_080df).
]]]
attr[seg000:88e1]: name = draw_subtitle_text_from_si; comment = [[[
    Render the expanded subtitle text at ds:si.
    lodsb the first byte: high bit set (>= 0x80) means nothing renderable, bail.
    Otherwise dec si and call loc_08b11 to lay out + draw. After drawing, if rand_bits[si] >= 0xfe also bail (post-render abort path).
]]]
attr[seg000:88f1]: name = expand_phrase_tokens; comment = [[[
    Expand a phrase/command string from ds:si into the 0xa840 buffer (es:di).
    Copies literal bytes through; bytes 0xe0..0xfd are phrase-pack references that index a sub-string at ss:[47b4h] + offset and rep movsb its bytes in. 0xfe is a soft separator; 0xff terminates. After each phrase expansion, inserts a 0x20 unless followed by 0xff.
    On return ds:si = the expanded text at ss:a840.
]]]
attr[seg000:8944]: type = code; name = format_interpolated_string
attr[seg000:8b10]: type = code
attr[seg000:8b11]: name = draw_subtitle_body; comment = [[[
    Main subtitle render: layout + draw the expanded text at ds:si.
    loc_08c8a: restore any prior subtitle area (clear/restore saved fb2 rect).
    loc_08ccd: pick the bubble rect, fg color, padding, and layout flags based on voice_subtitle_mode / suppress_sky / lip_sync / book / etc.
    draw_speech_bubble: optionally paint the bubble background; always seed pen + budget vars.
    loc_08df0: randomised text-decoration cleanup.
    Then vertical centring (if data_04799 & 0x0c == 0x08), per-line pen position, and the byte-by-byte glyph loop with colour-swap (0x01), color-spec (0x06), tab (0x08), space-wrap, and CR handling.
]]]
attr[seg000:8c0e]: type = u8
attr[seg000:8c41]: targets = seg000:d096, seg000:d0ff, seg000:d12f, seg000:d16a
attr[seg000:8c8a]: name = subtitle_restore_prior; comment = [[[
    Restore the framebuffer area covered by the previously-drawn subtitle.
    ax = xchg with data_0479e (the saved bubble bp). If < 2 (no prior subtitle), return.
    voice_subtitle_mode != 0: vga_put_rect from si=0x4c60 (the saved pixel buffer) back into fb2 at the [1be2..] rect, then clear data_00008+1be2.
    Always: copy_rect_fb2_to_fb1 to restore fb1 inside that rect; if data_047c8 has a saved lip-sync overlay, redraw via loc_09bac; finally loc_0c4dd to update the cursor + screen rect.
]]]
attr[seg000:8ca9]: targets = segvga:014e
attr[seg000:8ccd]: name = subtitle_setup_layout; comment = [[[
    Pick the bubble rect, fg colour, paddings, and layout flags for the subtitle.
    Defaults: data_04799 (layout flags) = 9 (bit0 random-decoration on, bit3 vertical-centre); font_draw_fg_color = 0xf0.
    Branches by state, each setting bp to a layout descriptor (rect at bp[0..6]) and zeroing/keeping the 4784/4786/4788/478a paddings:
    data_046eb != 0: error-message bubble (bp = seg001:2244).
    current_lip_sync_resource_id == 0xff: free-form, picks rect at seg001:224c with paddings 0x48,0x10,8,8.
    data_000c6 != 0: book/document bubble (bp = seg001:2265, paddings 0x3c,0x32,0xa,0xa, fg=0x64).
    suppress_sky_240_255 != 0: night/intro2 subtitle strip at seg001:2275 (0,153,320,47), no padding, fg=6.
    voice_subtitle_mode == 0: text mode, bp = seg001:223c, paddings 0x10,0x10,1,0, fg=0xf.
    Else (voice mode with lip-sync): scan a 3-entry table at seg001:2224 picking the first rect whose height fits the current line count.
]]]
attr[seg000:8e16]: name = layout_subtitle_lines; comment = [[[
    Word-wrap the formatted subtitle text (ds:si) into the per-line table at 0xa9d0.
    Walks bytes one at a time:
    high bit (>= 0x80): end of text. Commit current line if any, write terminator, store line count at [0xa9d0].
    0x0d carriage return: commit line, advance to next.
    0x20 space: skip (word separator).
    Else: scan one word via loc_08ed3 (returns cx = pixel width). cx += 6 (interword pad). If it fits in remaining width (bx = data_0478f), append; else start a new line (commit + reset bx).
    The written entries at 0xa9d2 onward are 8-byte records per word/break: see loc_08e9e (commit line) and loc_08b91 (the read side).
]]]
attr[seg000:8e9e]: name = commit_subtitle_layout_line; comment = [[[
    Commit the current word run to the per-line table at es:di and reset state for the next line.
    Write dl (word count this line) as a u16.
    If word count > 0: compute the inter-word stretch (remaining budget bx / (words-1)) + 6, store as the per-word advance, then store dx (=0) as line padding.
    dh++ (total line count), dl = 0 (words per new line), bx = subtitle_text_width_budget for the fresh budget.
]]]
attr[seg000:8ed3]: name = measure_word_width; comment = [[[
    Measure the pixel width of one word from ds:si in the currently-selected font.
    Walks bytes until 0x20 (space), 0x0d (CR) or high-bit (end of text); accumulates per-glyph widths from [_word_23C50_font_width_table] (tall or small font, set by font_select_tall_font / font_select_small_font).
    In-band control bytes inside a word:
    0x06 = colour-spec (skip next byte).
    0x08 = switch to the alternate font width table (0xceec).
    0x01..0x05/0x07/0x09+ = pass through (no width).
    Returns cx = total width in pixels, si advanced to the terminator byte.
]]]
